  "query_preview": "..\nAn approaching upper-level low will continue transporting \nmoisture into region, producing cloudy skies Saturday and \npossible rain across the northeast portion of Montana beginning \nSunday afternoon and lasting overnight. Precipitation totals will\nrange between 0.01\" and 0.25\".\n\nSustained winds of 20 mph with potential gusts to 40 mph \nassociated with the passage of the aforementioned low will likely \nresult in conditions reaching Lake Wind Advisory criteria. Rough \nconditions will begin late Sunday afternoon, relax overnight, and \nresume for the duration of Monday. Wave heights have the potential\nto reach 4.5'.\n\nTuesday Moving Forward:\nA weak ridging pattern will take place over Montana, although a\nbrief influx of moisture will pose chances for showers overnight \nTuesday and into Wednesday. There is uncertainty on rain amounts, \nbut expect less than 0.05\" at any given location as of the latest \nforecast. Beyond Tuesday, skies are anticipated to clear while \ntemperatures warm slightly under continued weak ridging.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nThere is moderate confidence in rain amounts through Tuesday.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence of sustained winds at or\nabove 20 mph on Sunday and Monday across Fort Peck Lake.\n\nDON",
